National Air Defense Shield: Full Supply Chain Proposal (Raw Materials to Final Domestic Installation)
Executive Summary
This comprehensive proposal outlines an end-to-end industrial base and supply chain strategy required to fabricate, assemble, test, deploy, and bolt down a multi-tier integrated air and missile defense architecture for the United States homeland ("Golden Dome").


The architecture seamlessly unifies four critical operational realms across all defensive layers:


* Information Realm (ISR): Orbital, air, sea, and ground sensors providing continuous early warning and tracking.
* Decision Realm (BMS): Command and control nodes utilizing automated threat evaluation and battle management logic.
* Communication Realm (C4ISR): Ultra-secure, low-latency, anti-jam tactical data links and backhaul networks.
* Kinetic Response Realm: Layered interception options including Ground-Based Interceptors (GBI), Terminal High Altitude Area Defense (THAAD), Aegis BMD, Patriot PAC-3 MSE, and Tamir/Iron Dome short-range systems.


