Tier 3: Communication & Network Infrastructure
Ensuring low-latency link stability and uncompromised command connectivity across all geographic defense sectors.


* Tactical Data Links: Integration of high-bandwidth Link-16 terminals, Integrated Air and Missile Defense Battle Command System (IBCS) relay adapters, and anti-jam Software Defined Radios (SDR) capable of dynamic spectrum hopping.
* Secure Backhaul Network: Construction of dedicated, redundant domestic military-grade fiber-optic rings protected by EMP-hardened conduit routing, complemented by Advanced Extremely High Frequency (AEHF) and MILSTAR satellite communication (SATCOM) surface transceivers.


________________


Tier 4: Quality Assurance, Acceptance & Environmental Testing
Every integrated unit undergoes strict military-standard qualification protocols prior to deployment.


* Environmental Stress Screening: Full-spectrum MIL-STD-810H and MIL-STD-461G compliance validation covering extreme thermal shock, random vibration profiles, blowing sand/dust resistance, salt fog corrosion, and electromagnetic interference (EMI) suppression.
* Hardware-in-the-Loop (HWIL) & Static Testing: HWIL testing within integrated anechoic chambers, radar cross-section (RCS) verification, dynamic target simulation, and static motor test firings under full thrust loads.


